==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 4~20 seconds<sup>120f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 4~20 seconds<sup>120f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 12~40 seconds<sup>360f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory|Gories]] spawn, delay 12~40 seconds<sup>360f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bore]] spawns as the boss.
**8 [[Znache]]s spawn, delay 6.67~54 seconds<sup>200f~1,620f</sup>.
**5 [[Zomboe]]s spawn, delay 13.33~54 seconds<sup>400f~1,620f</sup>.
**3 [[Zory|Zories]] spawn, delay 20~25.33 seconds<sup>600f~760f</sup>.
**1 [[Dread Bore]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The best way to deal with this stage is to stall Bore, then deal with the burrowing Dread Bore & co. using [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]]. To make this possible, one should spam [[Viking Cat (Rare Cat)|Maximum the Fighters]] and [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCats]], then stop as the units get close to the base; this way, Dread Bore will be alone in the front and you can kill it with [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cats]] (or [[Sarukani (Uber Rare Cat)|Sarukani]] if you have him) and [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Weedwacker Cats]] while Bore is busy. If you are fast enough, you can just resume the Maximum spam with added Li'l Flying Cats for an easy win. If Dread Bore isn't dead yet, your best bet is to add Maximum as a meatshield with a single iCat and hope that Dread Bore is Zombie-Killed; otherwise you can spam strong [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Reds]] and kill Bore first.

